\pard\sa120\sb120\fs32\b Connect-OneView\b0{\*\bkmkstart connect-oneview}{\*\bkmkend connect-oneview}\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Description\b0{\*\bkmkstart description}{\*\bkmkend description}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 This is a connection-focused alias for Test-ServerConnectivity. It validates network reachability and performs authentication in a single step, leaving an active OneView session available for subsequent commands (Get-OneViewServerList, Get-OneViewConnectionStatus, etc.). On a live run the appliance host is taken verbatim from -OneViewHost and credentials are entered interactively at the prompt. Config files are never read during a live run. The OneView session persists for the remainder of the PowerShell session. Use Disconnect-OneView to explicitly close it.\par
